# Commit a finished plan

Last step of every plan. Write it into the plan (plan mode) and run it when the plan is done (agent execution). Decide yourself. Do not ask. Do not push.

## When to commit

Commit when the change is more than 5 files, or fewer files but still a new flow, new backend behavior, or a multi-part UI.

Leave small work uncommitted: under 5 files, a minor UI tweak, copy edit, one-off fix, or a rule update.

## What to commit

- Stage only files this plan created or edited, including a cross-cutting edit.
- Leave other dirty and untracked files unstaged.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, keys); warn instead.
- If the plan changed no files, do not create an empty commit.

## Message

One line: `type: description`. Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `doc`, `chore`. Short lowercase description, same voice as `git log`.

```text
feat: xyz added
```

## How

Follow the repo git safety protocol. In parallel: `git status`, `git diff` (staged and unstaged), recent `git log`. Stage the plan's files by path. Commit with a HEREDOC. Then `git status` to confirm the commit and that unrelated local changes are still unstaged.

## Lint, typecheck, and build

Write these commands into the plan as the last verify step. Run them once at the end of every implementation, including work from a plan. ESLint is not a typecheck. Vite HMR and `vite-plugin-checker` overlay are not a substitute for `npx tsc --noEmit`. Treat a type overlay as a failure. After toolchain or typecheck changes, restart `npm run dev`; do not reuse a leftover CRA/`react-scripts` process on port 3000.

Plan-file-only or docs-only edits skip this pass. If a touched package has no matching command, skip that command and say so.

| Touched paths | Lint | Typecheck | Build |
|---|---|---|---|
| `src/**` | `npm run lint` | `npx tsc --noEmit` | `npm run build` |
| `functions/**` | `npm run lint --prefix functions` | skip (no tsconfig) | skip |
| `appScript/**` | `npx eslint appScript` | skip (JS) | skip |

Fix every error that pass reports. Do not treat unused-import, missing antd/MUI exports, or `Select`/`DatePicker` callback types as overlay noise. Do not re-run the full test suite. The user will run tests. Domain tests stay in `.cursor/rules/run-domain-tests.mdc`.
